  {
   "date": "0801-12-25",
   "type": "action_narrative",
   "title": "Odo Seized, but the Court Whispers",
   "description": "On Christmas Day, 801, a year after the crowning in Rome, Karl gave the order and Odo was taken. The guards moved swiftly and the count was bound and led to a cell before he could rally his followers. The deed itself succeeded: Odo lies imprisoned, his household scattered and his influence broken for now. Yet the arrest did not stay quiet. Servants had seen the soldiers cross the courtyard during the feast, and by nightfall the palace murmured about the king's suspicion and the lack of any open hearing. Odo's kin and friends among the nobles remembered the humiliation, and Odo himself, from behind the bars, cursed Karl's name and swore that the charge was a pretext. Karl kept his composure, and the court dared not speak against him openly, but the bitterness lingered. The king gained safety from one rival at the price of Odo's lasting hatred and a shadow of distrust in the hall.",
   "participants": [
    "karl",
    "generated-courtier-1"
   ]
